    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Welcome to Gandhinagar, India’s Tree Capital and Gujarat’s thoughtfully planned administrative heart. Designed with a rare balance of order and openness, the city offers a refreshing contrast to crowded urban centres. Tree-lined boulevards stretch beneath vast skies, public spaces feel unhurried, and the rhythm of daily life is calm and measured, allowing modern governance to exist in harmony with nature.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Named after Mahatma Gandhi, Gandhinagar is strategically located on the Delhi–Mumbai industrial corridor, just 23 kilometres north of Ahmedabad. With an impressive 54 percent green cover, it is widely regarded as Asia’s greenest capital city. The city is divided into 30 well-planned, self-sufficient sectors that function like mini townships, connected by wide, traffic-light boulevards. Buildings often recede behind dense canopies of trees, creating an uncluttered skyline where peace, greenery, and efficient urban planning come together seamlessly..",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Gandhinagar presents a compelling mix of spirituality, heritage, and culture, led by the magnificent BAPS Swaminarayan Akshardham Temple , a pink-sandstone marvel dedicated to Lord Swaminarayan, celebrated for its intricate carvings, serene gardens, exhibitions, and evening musical fountain and laser shows. The city’s historical depth is equally evident at the Adalaj Stepwell , a 15th-century Indo-Islamic masterpiece whose beautifully carved subterranean chambers remain naturally cool, and at the striking Dandi Kutir Museum , a salt-mound-inspired structure that vividly narrates Mahatma Gandhi’s life and the legacy of the Dandi March through immersive, technology-driven displays.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Nature and leisure complete the experience at Indroda Nature Park , often called India’s Jurassic Park, where dinosaur replicas, fossil exhibits, and impressive skeletal remains offer a journey through deep time. For a quieter escape, Aalloa Hills Resort provides a tranquil riverside setting with an adventure golf course, rich birdlife, Ayurvedic wellness therapies, and outdoor activities, making it an ideal blend of relaxation and recreation.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Navratri (September-October): Nine magical nights transform Gandhinagar into a kaleidoscope of colours. Thousands of people perform Garba and Dandiya Raas in traditional outfits at venues like Gandhinagar Cultural Forum Ground, and infectious energy and community spirit create unforgettable cultural immersion.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Uttarayan (January 14): This uniquely Gujarati phenomenon fills the skies with kites from dawn till dark, marking winter's turn to summer. Everyone takes to the rooftops for friendly aerial battles! People seek favoured kite-makers for strong, resilient kites with springy bamboo frames. Families savour Undhiyu and sesame sweets while thousands of kites dance against blue skies.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Authentic Gujarati cuisine balances sweet, spicy, and tangy flavours:",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "● Gujarati Thali: Complete feast with dal, kadhi, seasonal vegetables, rotli, rice, and sweets—unlimited servings",
      "source": {
