    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Most eateries are vegetarian and family-friendly, offering mild-spice versions for travelers.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Gandhinagar experiences pleasant weather for most of the year, with each season offering its own appeal. Winter, from October to February, is the best time to visit, as the climate is cool and comfortable, making it ideal for sightseeing, nature walks, and enjoying local festivals. The monsoon season, spanning July to September, transforms the city into a lush green landscape, with mild showers enhancing its natural beauty and refreshing atmosphere. Summer, from March to June, can be warm, but the city’s abundant tree cover and well‑planned green spaces help keep conditions manageable for visitors and residents alike.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Air: The nearest airport, Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport in Ahmedabad (18 km), connects Gandhinagar to major global destinations including the USA, UK, Middle East, and Southeast Asia.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Rail: The Gandhinagar Capital Railway Station (GNC) in Sector 14 is well connected with express trains like Shanti Express and Haridwar Mail.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "By Road: Excellent highways link Gandhinagar to Ahmedabad, Vadodara, and beyond. GSRTC buses, private operators, and taxis ensure seamless travel.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Swaminarayan Akshardham: The mandir is constructed entirely from pink sandstone without the use of steel, following traditional ancient temple-building techniques.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Dandi Kutir Museum: Designed in the form of a giant salt mound, the museum symbolically reflects Mahatma Gandhi’s iconic Dandi March.",
      "source": {
        "source_name": "Incredible India - Gandhinagar",
        "source_url": "https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/gujarat/gandhinagar",
        "retrieved_at": "2026-09-22T18:36:26.205424+00:00",
        "source_type": "official_tourism_page"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Adalaj ki Vav: Despite being over 500 years old, the stepwell remains naturally cool due to its unique five-level, inward-sloping architecture.",
